<h2>Important Owner Information</h2>

<div style="background: #fff3cd; border: 1px solid #ffc107; padding: var(--space-4); margin: var(--space-4) 0;">
  <strong>WARNING:</strong> Termite management systems require ongoing maintenance
  and regular inspections to remain effective.
</div>

<h3>Your Responsibilities</h3>

<ol>
  <li>
    <strong>Annual Inspections:</strong> Engage a licensed pest inspector to conduct
    annual termite inspections of your property.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Maintain the System:</strong> Do not disturb, damage, or breach the
    termite management system through excavation, landscaping, or construction.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Maintain Clearances:</strong> Keep gardens, mulch, and soil at least
    75mm below the weep holes and damp proof course.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Report Issues:</strong> If you notice termite activity or damage to
    the system, contact a licensed pest controller immediately.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Keep Records:</strong> Maintain all inspection reports and warranty
    documents for future reference and property transfer.
  </li>
</ol>

<h2>Acknowledgement</h2>

